        "original_id": "95b38fee-56e5-5207-8b1c-5ceab02525f9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Wagner, Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Set Svanholm, Lorenzo Quaglio\n- Works: Siegfried, Der Ring des Nibelungen, Idomeneo\n- Places: Mannheim, Munich\n- Roles: operatic tenor\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Wagner composed Siegfried, WWV 86C, as the third of the four music dramas in Der Ring des Nibelungen.\n- Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart composed Idomeneo, K. 366, as an Italian-language opera seria.\n- Lorenzo Quaglio worked mainly in Mannheim and Munich, and he designed the first production of Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart's opera Idomeneo.\n- Set Svanholm was a Swedish operatic tenor who was considered the leading Tristan and Siegfried of the first decade after World War II.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
